{
 "id": "subject-questions",
 "title": "Subject questions (Who called? What happened?)",
 "level": "B1",
 "unit": "12C",
 "units": [
  "12C"
 ],
 "en": "<p>When <b>who / what / which</b> is the <b>subject</b> (the person or thing that does the action), we <b>don't use do / does / did</b>: <i><b>Who called</b> you? <b>What happened</b>? <b>Which team won</b>?</i></p><p>When who / what is the <b>object</b>, we use the auxiliary as usual: <i><b>Who did you call</b>? <b>What did</b> she <b>say</b>?</i></p><p>Compare: <i>Who <b>loves</b> Aliya? (Someone loves Aliya — who?) / Who <b>does</b> Aliya <b>love</b>? (Aliya loves someone — who?)</i></p><p>The verb in a subject question is usually singular: <i>Who <b>works</b> here? Who <b>has</b> the key?</i></p>",
 "ru": "Вопрос к подлежащему (кто сделал?) — без do/does/did: Who called you? What happened? Вопрос к дополнению (кого? что?) — с do/does/did: Who did you call? What did she say? Глагол после who — в ед. числе: Who works here?",
 "boss": {
  "situation": "Write 6 questions for an incident review. Use at least 3 subject questions (Who reported…? What happened…?) and 3 object questions.",
  "samples": [
   "What happened on the night of the incident?",
   "Who reported the problem first?",
   "Which control failed?",
   "Who did you inform after that?",
   "What did the security team do?",
   "When did the system start working again?"
  ]
 },
